abstract = {The demand for cloud computing resources has led to a rise in critical problems related to load balancing, which is responsible for assigning tasks in cloud computing. Many dynamic and static load-balancing algorithms have been implemented to achieve the goals of users. Machine Learning models can predict future traffic patterns and resource demands based on historical data. This predictive analysis helps in distributing loads efficiently in anticipation of spikes or changes in traffic. This paper presents a comparative study of various predictive load balancing algorithms, evaluating their strengths, limitations, and suitability for diverse workload patterns and system architectures. By leveraging predictive load balancing algorithms effectively, organizations can optimize resource utilization, enhance performance, and ensure high availability in cloud computing environments.},
